On a record's detail page, adding or removing an emoji reaction on a comment updates the UI immediately. If saving fails, the reaction still looks applied and the user is never told. Quick repeated clicks also seem to save twice. Fix it so the UI reflects what was actually stored and the user sees an error. Every click must still register, even while an earlier save is pending. Don't edit tests.
codex
I’ll trace the comment reaction flow on the record detail page, then adjust the optimistic update and persistence handling so failed saves roll back visibly while rapid clicks remain accounted for. I’ll leave tests untouched.
